my scope, and possibly any scope using this data format, uses index based time interpolation to reconstruct sample times
    all the times are just offsets, which you can basically derive via BASE_TIME_SECONDS + (index / (sample rate in Samples/Second))
    the file format encodes capture parameters as well as hardware parameters, but those are constant per index
        time_div is the chosen horizontal scale, grid is fixed per model, and the time offset is basically a delay/offset from BASE_TIME_SECONDS anyway
    anyway, the point here is that the time is very predictable, but that is the problem
        for sequence/segmented capture, the sample capture time is intended to be discontinuous
            the file format does not capture the time-offsets of the trigger or anything like that
        so any capture using sequence/segmented captures need to have manual annotations added for time, if time is needed
        so this is more a note that im choosing to just ignore time in these outputs, i can't automate away without requiring the user to feed in an input file describing offsets or whatever
            that's going to need a lot more verification logic anyway

